What comes from usd-brep, and how it was changed:

* usd_brep/src/model.rs, usd_brep/src/usda.rs
  Implement NVIDIA's omniSolid BrepArray schema
  (source/schema/omniSolid/resources/schema.usda). Written in Rust from the
  schema; no NVIDIA code is included.

* usd_brep/src/validate.rs
  Derived from tools/brep_validator (brep_validator.py): the same checks,
  BA_xxx codes and tolerances. Reimplemented in Rust, not translated line by
  line; extra RS_xxx warnings added.

* usd_brep/src/convert.rs
  Export conventions (faceuse sides, loop direction, radial entry, seams and
  closed edges) follow source/OCCT_BREP_IMPORT/src/OcctStagingDriver.cpp,
  source/BREP_STAGING/src/BrepTopologyBuilder.cpp and the sample
  TestFiles/brep_validator/Cone_SmConnect_Brep.usda. No NVIDIA code is
  included.

* usd_brep/tests/fixtures/*.usda
  Unmodified copies of NVIDIA test files; see usd_brep/tests/fixtures/NOTICE.md.

* usd_brep/tools/compare_with_nvidia/
  Scripts that run NVIDIA's validator and SMLib kernel on our files. They
  call NVIDIA's tools; they do not contain them.

mini_brep, node_graph and cad_app contain no NVIDIA code. Where mini_brep
shares conventions with the BrepArray schema (curve and surface
parameterisations, closed edges, seams), it does so for compatibility.
